@lvxianchao/dsh-video-preview README · Use：1. Type `@` in the composer and pick a video file (or open one from the workspace changes).
2. Click the file reference; the right sidebar opens a player and starts muted playback.
3. Drag, unmute, go fullscreen with the native controls. Seeking fetches only the bytes around the new position.

@lvxianchao/dsh-video-preview README · How it works：The renderer uses `loading: "renderer"`, so the preview framework never performs a complete-byte read for video files — that is what removes the platform's 32 MB complete-file cap from the video path.

The browser half needs no build step — it is a module in the host loader's own format:

```js
window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id: "@lvxianchao/dsh-video-preview", factory: (require) => { /* … */ } });
```

@lvxianchao/dsh-video-preview README · Development：`main` is the release branch: it only carries code that has been released and tagged. Day-to-day work happens on `dev` and lands on `main` when a release is cut.

```bash
git checkout dev
